 and OpenRouter-derived data are **not**. Verified BOTH directions through the real publisher.\n- **Sparse-aware composite:** computed only where component coverage exists; coverage/missing shown explicitly â€” no false-authority single black-box index.\n- **Schema fix (BLOCKER):** live `model_benchmarks` had `source_url`/`scored_at`/`observed_at`/`contamination_flag` but **no `source`/`license`** column, and `benchmark_scraper.py` inserted without them. Fixed via migration `0027_benchmark_provenance.sql` (idempotent; schema.sql mirrored); single insert chokepoint `roles/benchmark_ingest.py::insert_benchmark` enforces CC5 provenance.\n- **Process:** EXECUTE â†’ orchestrator-run gate â†’ 2 reviewers (E = CC1/CC5 provenance **GO**; F = ingester/composite/cards **NO-GO**, 1 BLOCKER + 1 MAJOR with failing repro) â†’ FIX â†’ re-gate â†’ orchestrator re-verify.\n- **Gate:** 1108 â†’ **1120 passed** (+12 additive; same 1 pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure, untouched).\n\n**Wave 5 â€” Minimal, honest adoption (decisions + labels) (NS3, deliberately small) â€” GREEN 2026-06-12**\n- Decision content rendered as report items for top candidates (what-it-is / fit / recommendation+confidence / advantages / risks / provenance / effort); **recommendation is a non-authoritative suggestion, never a consensus verdict**.\n- **`decisions` table** records accept/decline/snooze and doubles as the label source feeding Wave 2's deferred weight-validation.\n- **No Helping-Hand auto-plumbing yet** â€” n=7 forbids automation; auto-adoption is a **future gate at nâ‰¥30**.\n- **Delivered:** migration `0028_decisions.sql` â€” `decisions(id, artifact_id FK, decision_type CHECK IN ('adopt','defer','reject','retire'), reason, explicit_label, explicit_confidence, made_at, made_by_session_id, recorded_at)`.\n- **Process:** EXECUTE â†’ orchestrator-run gate â†’ 2 reviewers (I = CC1/Â§B-2/anti-test-weakening; J = capture correctness + production-safety; **both GO**) â†’ 1 bounded hardening FIX â†’ re-gate.\n- **Gate:** 1135 â†’ **1152 passed** (+17 additive; same 1 pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure).\n\n---\n\nA few notes on grounding: the anchors give detail on **W3 and W5 only** â€” W1, W2, and W4 are named in the sequence and North-Star matrix but no implementation/gate detail was supplied here, so I haven't claimed any. Both reported gates carry the **same single pre-existing unrelated `runs` failure**, explicitly left untouched, with all added tests being additive.\n\nWant me to pull the W1/W2/W4 detail from the actual member documents to complete the picture?"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4260,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":30313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59e9abe5-e359-4284-a82a-21afd152a4a9","uuid":"1efc17d1-a7e5-40ec-bf0b-0ccefaabf16a","request_id":"req_011Cc9WdYC6XSBxyyGK6i4fX"}
